      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIMS",
          "content": "We aimed to assess the safety and performance of a novel sirolimus-eluting stent with biodegradable polymer under real-world conditions."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "METHODS AND RESULTS",
          "content": "This prospective, multicentre, observational, all-comers registry enrolled 1,356 patients. The primary endpoint was target lesion failure at 12 months: it occurred in 5.1% (95% CI: 4.0-6.4) of patients in the overall population and in 7.7% (95% CI: 5.5-10.9), 5.8% (95% CI: 4.2-8.1), 1.8% (95% CI: 0.2-11.8) and 7.2% (95% CI: 5.1-10.0) of patients with diabetes mellitus, small vessels, chronic total occlusion and acute myocardial infarction, respectively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "This novel stent platform demonstrated good clinical outcomes in an all-comers population, even in predefined high-risk groups. ClinialTrials.gov identifier: NCT01553526"
        }
      ]},
